  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Home Cinema Foyer",
    "overview": "Arr's web app is one calm feed on a warm cream page: white rounded cards, ink-green text, a single teal for action and arrival, a friendly round typeface, and the mascot as the brand mark. It is the same world as the Arr website, carried into a phone-first, single-column app. It reads like a household noticeboard for a TV room, not an admin console.\n\nThe page answers one question, \"is my thing coming?\". Search is pinned at the top; below it the feed deals out sections. Each row is a title tile or date chip, a title, and one next fact. Colour carries meaning: teal says here or act, coral says needs you, sun-yellow says a date.\n\nDensity is relaxed: 44px minimum targets, 18px card corners, 2px borders. Dark mode is the website's night palette, not an inversion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream page, white cards, every card outlined in a 2px warm line.",
      "Teal is the only action colour; coral is reserved for \"Needs you\".",
      "Nunito (self-hosted) at weights 500 to 800; bold, rounded, no thin weights.",
      "Single centred column, max 680px; bottom tab bar on phones, top-right tabs on desktop.",
      "Title tiles (coloured initials) stand in for artwork; no posters yet.",
      "The four-stop journey line is the signature element."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Coral Means Needs-You Rule",
        "body": "Coral appears only on rows in \"Needs you\" and error messages. If an item is not waiting on a person, it is not coral.",
